# Columns: Break with Before: column or After: column moves the content to the next column.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Columns · Column breaks
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: day
			Typography:
				Bold: true
				Color: accent
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 4 0
	Section:
		Text: Columns
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Column breaks
		Paragraph: Inside a `Columns`, `Break` with `Before: column` starts a box at the top of the next column, and `After: column` sends what follows there. With `page` instead of `column` the jump is to the next page.
			Style: intro
		Text: Before: column on each day after the first
			Style: label
		Columns:
			Column count: 3
			Gap: 16
			Separator: 0.5
			Separator color: rule
			Text: Friday
				Style: day
			Paragraph: Opening of the market at nine.
			Text: Saturday
				Style: day
				Break:
					Before: column
			Paragraph: Walk along the river, from the old bridge.
			Paragraph: Lunch at the mill.
			Text: Sunday
				Style: day
				Break:
					Before: column
			Paragraph: Closing concert in the square.
		Text: After: column on the first paragraph
			Style: label
		Columns:
			Column count: 2
			Gap: 16
			Separator: 0.5
			Separator color: rule
			Paragraph: This paragraph ends the first column, because it declares After: column.
				Break:
					After: column
			Paragraph: This one starts the second column, although the first one had room for it.
